sia-brain - the local model of SIEOS's assistant, sia

sia-brain is built on Ministral 3 3B Instruct (2512), an open model by
Mistral AI, released under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the LICENSE
file next to this one):
    https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512

What SIEOS changed: the file sia-brain.gguf is Mistral AI's own GGUF of the
model in BF16 (Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-BF16.gguf, SHA-256
17ef932bea952e007f9dad63151da5699132ec513d1033d618df7382e24aa3ee),
quantized to IQ4_XS with llama.cpp's llama-quantize, guided by an importance
matrix computed with llama-imatrix on SIEOS's own documentation and sources.
The weights were not trained or fine-tuned further; the vision encoder is not
included.  The name sia-brain is SIEOS's: Mistral AI does not endorse SIEOS,
and no trademark of Mistral AI is licensed here.

It runs on llama.cpp (the package llama-cpp, MIT License).
